# 998 Web Designs design system (998webdesigns-com-site repo)

This rule encodes the canonical brand tokens for **998webdesigns.com** - a standalone Bear LLC product brand for $998 flat-fee custom websites. By design, the page does NOT reference SlatePress (positioning split: SlatePress is the marketing-system tier, 998 is the entry-level one-off site tier). Visually the two brands stay close enough to feel familial without sharing copy.

The source of truth for these tokens is the `:root` block at the top of `index.html`. If they ever drift, this rule should be updated to match - the live file wins.

## Canonical tokens

```css
:root{
  --bg:#FFFFFF;             /* page canvas - pure white */
  --ink:#0A0A0A;            /* primary text, near-black */
  --ink-soft:#3A3D42;       /* secondary text */
  --slate:#6B6A73;          /* tertiary text */
  --rule:#E5E7EB;           /* default 1px borders */
  --blue:#2563EB;           /* PRIMARY brand blue - logo "/" + primary CTAs */
  --blue-deep:#1D4ED8;      /* hover state */
  --blue-soft:#EFF3FF;      /* tinted backgrounds, badges */
}
```

## Type stack

**Inter only.** Single sans-serif throughout.

```css
font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, system-ui, sans-serif;
```

## Cardinal rules for 998webdesigns-com-site

- **Pure white canvas (`--bg #FFFFFF`).** Mercury-clean - the brand identity is "single page, single price, single CTA." Don't add gradient backgrounds, hero imagery, or dark-mode sections.
- **Brand blue (`--blue` #2563EB) is the one accent.** Same blue as the SlatePress family (Bear LLC house color). Logo `/`, primary CTAs (currently the `mailto:` to `hello@998webdesigns.com`), focus rings.
- **Zero SlatePress mention.** This is positioning discipline, not just visual. Don't add SlatePress logos, copy, or cross-links in the page UI. (Internal docs / repo READMEs can reference the parent Bear LLC structure - just not the live page.)
- **No new hex codes.** Stick to the 8-token set. Adding decoration will dilute the "$998, one site, one price" message.
- **No gradient buttons, no carousels, no Lorem ipsum, no emoji in production UI.**
- **One offer, one price.** $998 flat. If the offer evolves (form-capture replacement of mailto, Stripe checkout button, schema.org JSON-LD blocks), see `whats-next.md` items 8-12 in the workspace root for the queued upgrades.

## Pricing

$998 one-time flat-fee. Distinct from SlatePress Foundation pricing - no cross-repo pricing-sync rule applies. The $998 number appears in the brand name, the headline, the CTA copy, and the offer spec at `outputs/998webdesigns-form-capture-spec.md`. If pricing ever moves, all four touchpoints update together (and the domain rebrand becomes a hard problem).

## When designing or reviewing UI in this repo

Defer to the `premium-web-designer` Claude skill. When it fires:
1. Ask "What are we designing today?"
2. On the answer "998webdesigns.com" or any edit in this repo, load the tokens above.
3. Apply universal taste principles on top.
4. Produce code that references the brand's variable names (`--blue`, `--ink`, `--bg`) directly - never invent token names.
